<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rouran Khaganate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rouran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rouran Khaganate was a nomadic confederation that dominated the Mongolian steppe from the late fourth to the mid-sixth century CE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Göktürks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bumin-qaghan">Bumin</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina clan</a> were originally its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, and their revolt destroyed Rouran power in the 550s. The Gokturk Empire profile describes this rupture as the origin of the Göktürk state, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a> profile lists the Rouran among the steppe powers that inherited the Xiongnu military tradition.</p></div>
